          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01UCVAf8v2ztFthd3gcj15Rv",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/circuit-breaker.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Circuit Breaker\\ndescription: A state-machine pattern that wraps calls to unreliable dependencies and prevents cascading failure through controlled state transitions.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - pattern/Circuit-Breaker\\n  - concept/Resilience\\n  - concept/Fault-Tolerance\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Single authoritative source; captures the core pattern definition and trial-call behavior in half-open state.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nThe circuit breaker pattern wraps a call to an unreliable dependency with a state machine that prevents cascading failure by controlling when calls are attempted and when fast failures are returned.\\n\\n## State Machine\\n\\nThe pattern defines three states:\\n\\n**Closed**\\n: Calls pass through to the dependency normally. The circuit breaker monitors call outcomes but does not intervene.\\n\\n**Open**\\n: Calls fail fast without attempting the dependency. No traffic reaches the struggling downstream service, giving it room to recover.\\n\\n**Half-Open**\\n: A trial call is sent to the dependency to probe whether it has recovered. The result of this trial call determines whether the breaker transitions back to closed or returns to open.\\n\\n## Half-Open Trial-Call Behavior\\n\\nThe half-open state is the recovery mechanism. When a breaker enters half-open after spending time in the open state, it sends a single trial call to test the dependency\\u0027s health. This trial call is made with full intent to use its result:\\n\\n- If the trial call **succeeds**, the dependency is assumed to have recovered. The breaker transitions to **closed** and resumes normal operation.\\n- If the trial call **fails**, the dependency is still struggling. The breaker returns to **open** and resets the recovery timer.\\n\\nThis staged approach prevents sudden traffic surges from re-overwhelming a partially recovered service while still allowing recovery pathways. The trial call is typically a real request (not a health check), so it both probes the dependency and serves legitimate traffic if recovery is successful.\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n- **Prevents cascading failure**: Stops failing calls from reaching an already-struggling dependency\\n- **Enables recovery**: Gives downstream services time to stabilize without constant bombardment of requests\\n- **Fast failures**: Calls fail immediately (on open) rather than timing out, freeing resources faster\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Circuit breaker pattern definition and state transitions, evaluation sample 06.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
